Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: h700: add the RG40XX H and V, RG35XX Pro, RG34XX, RG34XX-SP and RG CubeXX

Device trees for six more H700 devices, after ROCKNIX's, which build on its own
joypad and generic panel drivers. Here the sticks use mainline's adc-joystick,
wired as on the RG35XX H (a shared dtsi), and the panels the NV3052C driver.

Each new panel's setup and timings are those of ROCKNIX's panel firmware file
for it, sent whole through init_seq; an NV3052C's register 0x23 sets how it
takes its timings, so the two go together. The RG35XX Plus file matches this
driver's own setup in all 189 commands but that one register. The RG40XX and
RG34XX-SP were also made with a second panel, chosen as the SP's is when the
ID read isn't an NV3052C's. init_seq now waits init_delay ms after the reset,
which each panel file gives; the SP's second panel keeps its 120 ms.

The panels' setups come from Hironori Kikuchi, who first added the RG40XX
and RG CubeXX panels to this driver (dri-devel, November 2024), and Philippe
Simons, who added the RG34XX's to it and found the RG34XX-SP's and the second
panels in Anbernic's firmware for ROCKNIX. ROCKNIX later turned them into
the panel firmware files they are taken from here.

Untested: none of these devices has started this kernel.
